The fork (mlx-omarchy, MLX 0.32.3 + Omarchy patches) inserted a
`const std::optional<array>& global_scale` parameter into gather_qmm before
`sorted_indices`; the pinned mlx-c @56b2d39 predates that and passes
`sorted_indices` (bool) in its place, which fails to compile. Every other
extended signature this mlx-c revision already matches the fork (quantize,
dequantize, qqmm all carry global_scale here). Shim: pass no global scale —
the C ABI has no surface for it yet.

--- a/mlx/c/ops.cpp
+++ b/mlx/c/ops.cpp
@@ -1501,5 +1501,7 @@
             (bits.has_value ? std::make_optional<int>(bits.value)
                             : std::nullopt),
             std::string(mode),
-            sorted_indices,
+            /* global_scale: no C ABI surface yet */
+            std::nullopt,
+            sorted_indices,
             mlx_stream_get_(s)));
